## What it reaches

`reaches` in the manifest declares what this Cog touches OUTSIDE the run —
declared, never inferred. It is empty in the starter.

When it is not empty, the Op runner issues a grant
(`openteams/op-grant [0.1]`) for the invocation and passes `--grant` beside
`--run-id`; this Cog **checks that grant itself** before every external call
and refuses without one (`no-grant`). The local host runs trusted code with
the owner's ambient credentials: the grant is checked by this code, and this
is not an enforced restricted environment.

Effects are recorded as they happen in the `--journal` the runner supplies
(append-only JSONL, fsynced per line), which this Cog reads FIRST on every
invocation so an effect already applied is never applied twice.

